For COLMAP conversion, NPA preserves each frame's actual camera-to-world poses
in `T_sensor_worlds`, including composition through downsampled camera parents.
The derived `npa_rig` group uses explicitly virtual identity camera-to-rig
calibrations and a merged world trajectory at disjoint virtual camera timestamps.
The converter preserves 1 FPS photographic ordering, shares timestamps with
downsampled aliases, and records original/new indices and image hashes. This
makes the native rig-interpolating consumer use each camera's actual world pose;
the earlier overlapping-timeline pose override was insufficient. These timestamps
are not capture time or physical rig motion. Original
poses, image bytes, calibration, masks and point records remain independently
audited; malformed or contradictory pose contracts fail before reconstruction.

Dataset bytes are fetched at runtime, never baked into the converter image.
Retain this attribution, the immutable source revision, source hashes and a
description of conversion/rig changes alongside derived runtime artifacts.
The live-matrix seeder writes source/attribution.json beside the original ZIP.
That sidecar is separate from the converter's conversion.json provenance.

